  "user_request_original": "Design an aperiodic multilayer dielectric stack on silicon substrate with air incidence. Stack structure: air | (hfo2 | SiO2 (Kischkat))_12 | si, exactly 24 layers total. Optimize individual layer thicknesses for all 24 layers, initialized with linear chirp from quarter-wave at 8000 nm (front) to quarter-wave at 13000 nm (back). Target: maximize mean emissivity in 8000-13000 nm band, minimize mean emissivity in 3000-5000 nm band, maximize spectral uniformity within 8000-13000 nm. Wavelength range for evaluation: 3000-13000 nm. Polarization: unpolarized (average TE and TM). Incidence angle: 0 degrees (normal). Material refractive indices from catalog datasets for hfo2, SiO2 (Kischkat), and si. Total layer count fixed at 24.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thicknesses of a 24-layer aperiodic air/HfO2/SiO2/Si stack (12 pairs) with linear chirp from 8000 nm to 13000 nm quarter-waves. Maximize mean absorptance/emissivity in 8000–13000 nm, minimize mean absorptance/emissivity in 3000–5000 nm, and enforce peak-to-valley uniformity in 8000–13000 nm using worst-case aggregation. Evaluate 3000–13000 nm at 0° normal incidence unpolarized.",
